Host build only — the firmware never calibrates the brake pressure sensor.

BrakePressureSensor_new() calls BrakePressureSensor_resetCalibration(), which
sets bps0_calibMin = bps0_calibMax = bps0->sensorValue. At construction that
sensor has not been read yet, so both bounds are 0 and `calibrated` stays
FALSE. BrakePressureSensor_update() then takes its uncalibrated branch every
cycle, forcing percent = 0 and brakesAreOn = FALSE: the brake pressure the sim
feeds in is thrown away and the VCU believes the brakes are never touched.

Pre-load the same bounds the sensor's own specMin/specMax already describe and
mark it calibrated. Same shape, and the same open question, as the throttle in
0003: ask the VCU team how the car gets a calibrated brake today. If the answer
is "a calibration routine", this patch goes away once the harness can drive
that routine instead.

Verified on the host with this patch applied — at apps = 50%, bps = 40 bar the
firmware now reads mv = 2070, percent = 0.400, brakesAreOn = 1 and raises
F_tpsbpsImplausible (faults = 0x400). Without it, percent stays 0.000 and the
fault never fires.

NOTE, and this is NOT something this patch can fix: the fault still does not
reduce torque. Both rear motors stay at full 35000 mA through the whole
implausibility. SafetyChecker_reduceTorque() computes multiplier = 0 correctly
and then discards it — the four lines that apply it to powertrain->motor_* are
commented out (safety.c, end of the function), disabled by upstream commit
4c164a7 "commenting out cutting off motors" and still commented at 5df1baf.
That is a firmware fix, not a host-build workaround, so it is deliberately not
patched here. See docs/problems.txt section C.

--- a/brakePressureSensor.c
+++ b/brakePressureSensor.c
@@ -48,6 +48,16 @@
     me->calibrated = FALSE;
     BrakePressureSensor_resetCalibration(me);
 
+    // SIL: nothing calibrates the brake on the host. resetCalibration() sets
+    // calibMin = calibMax = bps0->sensorValue, which is 0 before the first ADC
+    // read, so there is never a usable span and the brakes read permanently
+    // OFF -- EV.4.7 plausibility and regen can never be exercised. Preload the
+    // datasheet bounds and mark it calibrated, exactly as the throttle patch
+    // does in 0003.
+    me->bps0_calibMin = 450;
+    me->bps0_calibMax = 4500;
+    me->calibrated = TRUE;
+
     return me;
 }
 
